From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix build with OCaml 5: drop the Stream and Genlex modules

OCaml 5.0 removed `Stream` and `Genlex` from the standard library, so
`ocaml setup.ml -configure` fails with:

    File "src/oasis/OASISFileSystem.ml", line 107, characters 4-10:
    Error: Unbound module Stream

The obvious fix -- depending on `camlp-streams` -- is not available here.
`OASISFileSystem`, `BaseEnvLight`, `BaseEnv`, `BaseLog` and
`OASISSourcePatterns` are all part of the ocamlmod bundles that get
inlined into every project's `setup.ml` and `myocamlbuild.ml` (see
`BaseGenerate.ml` and `OCamlbuildPlugin.ml`). Those files are run by
plain `ocaml setup.ml`, without findlib and without packages, so the
uses of `Stream`/`Genlex` have to be removed rather than re-provided.

`OASISString.Genlex` replaces `Genlex.make_lexer` with a small
stdlib-only tokenizer. It lexes a whole string at once -- all five
grammars OASIS parses this way describe small, fully buffered files --
and returns each token with the line it starts on, which preserves the
"Malformed data file '%s' line %d" errors that the lazy `Stream.npeek`
idiom used to provide. `BaseLog` even gains correct line numbers, its
counter was never incremented.

It is placed before `(* END EXPORT *)` in `OASISString.ml`, and
`OASISString` precedes `BaseEnvLight` in every bundle, so it is
available both to the library and to the generated files.

Call sites:

  * `OASISFileSystem.stream_of_reader` becomes `string_of_reader`, and
    `host_fs#open_in` reads through `Bytes`/`input`. This also drops an
    off-by-one, the old `for _i = 0 to len` read `len + 1` characters.
  * `BaseEnvLight.load` takes `?content:string` instead of
    `?stream:char Stream.t`.
  * `BaseEnv.var_expand` and `BaseLog.load` walk a token list.
  * `OASISSourcePatterns.parse` uses a module alias, `Ident` and
    `String` are both token and expr constructors there.
  * `OASISUtils.split_command_line` uses an index cursor.
  * `OASISParse.from_stream` is removed. It only materialised the stream
    into a string and called `from_string`, and had no callers.

`setup.ml` and `myocamlbuild.ml` are patched by hand so that the tree
can bootstrap; they should be regenerated with `./Main.native setup`
once the build works. The two `Pervasives.compare` left in `setup.ml`
by the 0.4.11 generation are removed as well, they are equally fatal on
OCaml 5.

Tests use `Seq.iter`, as `OUnit2.assert_command`'s `~foutput` takes
a `char Seq.t` since ounit2 2.2.6. Minimum OCaml is now 4.02, for `Bytes`
and `really_input_string`.

